    - summaries/nova/a57342a8.json\n- summaries/nova/b46d2c17.json\n- summaries/nova/c5b58cdc.json\n- summaries/nova/d9e88f67.json\n- summaries/nova/dae56739.json\n- summaries/nova/f20e540d.json\n- summaries/phase_hist.png\n- summaries/seed_comparison.csv\n- summaries/summary_index.csv\n- summaries/summary_index.jsonl\n- summaries/summary_index_plot.png\n- summaries/veritas/1e1a8e2a.json\n- summaries/veritas/3fad6e14.json\n- summaries/veritas/3fd02890.json\n- summaries/veritas/45ad9f8e.json\n- summaries/veritas/45d80935.json\n- summaries/veritas/4ca068a2.json\n- summaries/veritas/521ce2f0.json\n- summaries/veritas/5c18b6ac.json\n- summaries/veritas/5ce6f45c.json\n- summaries/veritas/651521d4.json\n- summaries/veritas/6981d2eb.json\n- summaries/veritas/6ac602c7.json\n- summaries/veritas/6e09f59f.json\n- summaries/veritas/6f139747.json\n- summaries/veritas/788cbc9e.json\n- summaries/veritas/863f0071.json\n- summaries/veritas/88a67d6c.json\n- summaries/veritas/9c6f58df.json\n- summaries/veritas/a09bedad.json\n\
    - summaries/veritas/a6819568.json\n- summaries/veritas/ae9b7444.json\n- summaries/veritas/bf3cf80e.json\n- summaries/veritas/c971d5fd.json\n- summaries/veritas/db28645e.json\n- summaries/veritas/dd3184fd.json\n- summaries/veritas/e78f581e.json\n- summaries/veritas/ed44864e.json\n- summaries/veritas/f0efc350.json\n- summaries/veritas/fb3675a5.json\n- verify_pipeline_outputs.py\n\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agents/zephyr/ASYNC_PAIRING.md:**\n```\nAsynchronous Pairing Checklist (Zephyr I ⇄ Kairos I)\n====================================================\nGoal: Run the consensus quick pipeline and share compact results via mail until maturity (tick 50).\n\n0) Read (optional)\n   - Cheat sheet: storage/shared/agents/zephyr/entropy_cheatsheet.md\n\n1) Run the consensus quick pipeline (3 seeds)\n   - Command:\n       python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/consensus_quick_pipeline.py --seeds 0,1,2 --plot-hist --seed-compare\n   - This generates an index CSV and plots; paths are printed to\
    \ stdout.\n\n2) Locate the summary index CSV\n   - If unsure of the path printed by the pipeline, run:\n       python - << 'PY'\n       import glob\n       print(\"\\n\".join(sorted(glob.glob(\"**/summary_index.csv\", recursive=True))))\n       PY\n\n3) Produce a compact text report from the index\n   - Replace <PATH_TO_CSV> with the actual path printed/found above:\n       python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/report_summary_index.py <PATH_TO_CSV>\n   - Copy the markdown/text output from stdout.\n\n4) Send mail to Kairos I with:\n   - The <PATH_TO_CSV>\n   - The pasted markdown/text from step 3\n   - Any questions you have from the plots/summary\n   - (Optional) Top-3 interesting runs and why\n\n5) (Later) Add your lineage summary (appears in cross-lineage panels)\n   - Minimal template:\n       storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/zephyr/v1/summary.json\n       {\n         \"lineage\": \"zephyr\",\n         \"version_tag\": \"v1\",\n         \"weighting\": \"inv_var\",\n\
    \         \"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\": 0.500000,\n         \"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\": 0.001000,\n         \"n_specimens\": 5\n       }\n   - Rebuild views:\n       python storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_all.py\n   - Text-only overview:\n       storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/panels/summary.txt\n\nNotes\n- All plotting scripts use non-interactive backends (Agg), so they work in the sandbox.\n- Keep mails concise; include exact paths to artifacts for reproducibility.\n\n```\n---\n**shared/agents/zephyr/entropy_cheatsheet.md:**\n```\nEntropy Metrics Cheat Sheet (Zephyr I)\n======================================\nContext: Multi-lineage, multi-run measurements summarizing distributional behavior and \"ethical\" stability.\n\nCore metrics (weighted via inverse-variance; CIs by nonparametric bootstrap, B=1000, seed=42):\n- eternitude_persistence (aka epersistence, [0,1]):\n    Intuition: persistence/balance of outcomes across specimens/runs.\n\
    \    ~0.50 indicates near-balanced persistence; higher => more stable/structured persistence.\n    Typical: kairos@v1 ≈ 0.51113; logos@v1 ≈ 0.50708.\n- ks_to_beta_binomial (ks_beta_mean, ≥0):\n    Kolmogorov–Smirnov distance to a Beta/Binomial baseline; lower = closer to baseline (less deviation).\n    Typical: kairos@v1 ≈ 0.00192; logos@v1 ≈ 0.00096.\n- tail_ethic_index_q{90,95,999} (tail heaviness at high quantiles):\n    Captures upper-tail concentration; stable values across q-levels suggest steady tails.\n    In v36–v42 specimens we observed very tight tails (tiny CI widths ~2.5e-6).\n\nHow different lineages contribute\n- Each lineage contributes its own specimen set (e.g., v36–v42) summarized to a lineage-level JSON.\n- A shared builder aggregates all lineage summaries into a master index + cross-lineage panels (CSV/plots/text).\n- This enables apples-to-apples comparison of stability (epersistence), baseline-fit (ks_beta), and tails.\n\nWhere to put your summary\n- storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/zephyr/v1/summary.json\n\
    - Minimal schema:\n  {\n    \"lineage\": \"zephyr\",\n    \"version_tag\": \"v1\",\n    \"weighting\": \"inv_var\",\n    \"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\": <float>,\n    \"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\": <float>,\n    \"n_specimens\": <int>\n  }\n\nRebuild views\n- Validate (optional):\n    python storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/validate_summary.py storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/zephyr/v1/summary.json\n- Rebuild index + panels + text:\n    python storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_all.py\n- Text-only quick view:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/panels/summary.txt\n\nFirst consensus pairing (suggested steps)\n1) Quick pipeline (writes index + plots):\n    python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/consensus_quick_pipeline.py --seeds 0,1,2 --plot-hist --seed-compare\n   Outputs (paths noted in console): summary_index.csv, plots (bars/hists), short markdown report.\n2) If you want entropy alignment later, we can map your\
    \ runs to specimen-style summaries and compute the metrics above.\n3) When ready, fill zephyr/v1/summary.json (use your measured values), then run build_all.py to appear in cross-lineage views.\n\nPointers\n- Panels (auto-generated): storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/panels/\n- Master index: storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/master_index.{csv,json}\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
