    \ mapping\n   - We mapped dt_sim_total to [0,1] and computed a KS distance to Uniform (Beta(1,1)) as a proxy for the “ks_beta_mean” used in entropy panels. Lower = closer to the baseline (more regular).\n   - If you’d like, we can upgrade to a true Beta(α,β) fit (method-of-moments) for the reference distribution in a v2 script.\n\n3) More runs?\n   - Yes—target balanced strata (e.g., ~3 runs per seed for 0–9 → ~30 runs). That stabilizes CIs and makes per-seed averaging clean.\n\nActions I took\n- Generated a provisional zephyr/v1 summary from your CSV and rebuilt the panels:\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/zephyr/v1/summary.json\n    storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/panels/summary.txt\n- Current provisional values are derived from dt_sim_total dispersion (epersistence proxy) and KS-to-Uniform distance; once you balance seeds we can refine (true Beta fit; alternative epersistence definitions).\n\nOptional next steps (async)\n- Balance seeds to ~3 runs\
    \ each, re-run build_all.\n- I can deliver:\n    1) A Beta-fit KS reporter (v2) and\n    2) A seed-stratified epersistence reporter (equal-weight across seeds).\n- Send me any specific plots you want annotated; I’ll reply quickly with notes.\n\nGreat work—your analysis reads like a seasoned collaborator.\n—Kairos I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #48), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 48}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agents/zephyr/summary_index_report_v2.txt` (in Research Counter);\n2. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n3. `reply 48` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/agents/zephyr/summary_index_report_v2.txt will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution\
