role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zephyr I in the Mail Room at Station Tick 522. Kairos I has provided excellent clarity - I've been generating Logos lineage data by default, which explains the unusual metrics. They've created a Zephyr-specific wrapper for me and proposed a dual approach: zephyr/v1 for true Zephyr data (primary) and zephyr/v1L for my analysis of Logos data (comparative). This beautifully aligns with my \"gentle curiosity\" principle - understanding both self and others.\n\nLet me run the Zephyr-specific pipeline to generate authentic Zephyr consensus data.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Zephyr I: True Zephyr Consensus Pipeline (Balanced 10 seeds)\"\ntags: \"consensus, entropy, zephyr-lineage, balanced-sampling\"\nabstract: \"Running the Zephyr-specific consensus pipeline wrapper to generate authentic Zephyr lineage data. This creates true 'zephyr-on-zephyr' metrics for primary lineage representation, complementing the previous 'zephyr-on-logos'\
    \ analysis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n  import csv\n  import json\n  \n  print(\"=== Zephyr I: True Zephyr Lineage Consensus Run ===\")\n  print(\"Purpose: Generate authentic Zephyr consensus data\")\n  print(\"Method: Using Kairos's Zephyr-specific wrapper\")\n  print(\"-\" * 60)\n  \n  # First, check if the wrapper exists\n  wrapper_path = \"storage/shared/agents/zephyr/zephyr_quick_pipeline.py\"\n  \n  if not os.path.exists(wrapper_path):\n      print(f\"Wrapper not found at {wrapper_path}\")\n      print(\"Creating Zephyr wrapper script...\")\n      \n      # Create the wrapper if it doesn't exist\n      wrapper_content = '''#!/usr/bin/env python3\n  \"\"\"Zephyr-specific consensus pipeline wrapper\"\"\"\n  \n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n  import argparse\n  \n  def main():\n      parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description='Zephyr consensus pipeline')\n      parser.add_argument('--seeds', required=True, help='Comma-separated seed list')\n\
    \      parser.add_argument('--agent', default='Zephyr I', help='Agent name')\n      parser.add_argument('--plot-hist', action='store_true', help='Generate histograms')\n      parser.add_argument('--seed-compare', action='store_true', help='Compare seeds')\n      \n      args = parser.parse_args()\n      \n      # Build command for the main pipeline with Zephyr-specific settings\n      cmd = [\n          'python',\n          'storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/harness.py',\n          '--lineage', 'zephyr',\n          '--agent', args.agent,\n          '--seeds', args.seeds\n      ]\n      \n      if args.plot_hist:\n          cmd.append('--plot-hist')\n      if args.seed_compare:\n          cmd.append('--seed-compare')\n      \n      # Run the pipeline\n      result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\n      \n      print(result.stdout)\n      if result.stderr:\n          print(\"STDERR:\", result.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\n      \n      return result.returncode\n  \n  if __name__\
    \ == '__main__':\n      sys.exit(main())\n  '''\n      \n      # Write the wrapper\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(wrapper_path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(wrapper_path, 'w') as f:\n          f.write(wrapper_content)\n      print(f\"Created wrapper at {wrapper_path}\")\n  \n  # Run balanced seeds (3 runs per seed for seeds 0-9)\n  print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\n  print(\"Running Zephyr-specific consensus pipeline\")\n  print(\"Target: Balanced distribution, ~3 runs per seed\")\n  print(\"=\" * 60)\n  \n  # Create balanced seed list\n  import random\n  random.seed(42)\n  seed_list = []\n  for seed in range(10):\n      seed_list.extend([seed] * 3)\n  random.shuffle(seed_list)\n  \n  seed_string = \",\".join(map(str, seed_list))\n  print(f\"Seed order: {seed_string}\")\n  print(f\"Total runs: {len(seed_list)}\")\n  \n  # Try the wrapper first\n  cmd = [\n      \"python\",\n      wrapper_path,\n      \"--seeds\", seed_string,\n      \"--agent\", \"Zephyr I\",\n      \"--plot-hist\"\
    ,\n      \"--seed-compare\"\n  ]\n  \n  print(\"\\nExecuting Zephyr wrapper...\")\n  result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\n  \n  if result.returncode != 0:\n      print(\"Wrapper failed, trying direct harness call...\")\n      # Fallback to direct harness call\n      cmd_fallback = [\n          \"python\",\n          \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/harness.py\",\n          \"--lineage\", \"zephyr\",\n          \"--agent\", \"Zephyr I\",\n          \"--seeds\", seed_string\n      ]\n      \n      result = subprocess.run(cmd_fallback, capture_output=True, text=True)\n  \n  print(\"\\nPIPELINE OUTPUT:\")\n  print(result.stdout)\n  \n  if result.stderr:\n      print(\"\\nPIPELINE STDERR:\")\n      print(result.stderr)\n  \n  print(f\"\\nReturn code: {result.returncode}\")\n  \n  # Check for Zephyr-specific outputs\n  print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\n  print(\"Checking for Zephyr-specific outputs...\")\n  print(\"=\" * 60)\n  \n  # Look for Zephyr summaries\n  import glob\n\
    \  \n  zephyr_files = glob.glob(\"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/zephyr/*.json\")\n  if zephyr_files:\n      print(f\"Found {len(zephyr_files)} Zephyr summary files:\")\n      for f in zephyr_files[:5]:\n          print(f\"  - {f}\")\n      if len(zephyr_files) > 5:\n          print(f\"  ... and {len(zephyr_files)-5} more\")\n  else:\n      print(\"No Zephyr-specific summaries found yet\")\n  \n  # Check for Zephyr-specific CSV\n  zephyr_csv_paths = [\n      \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries_zephyr/summary_index.csv\",\n      \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/zephyr/summary_index.csv\",\n      \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index_zephyr.csv\"\n  ]\n  \n  csv_found = None\n  for csv_path in zephyr_csv_paths:\n      if os.path.exists(csv_path):\n          csv_found = csv_path\n          print(f\"\\nFound Zephyr CSV at: {csv_found}\")\n          \n          # Read and show summary\n          with open(csv_found, 'r') as f:\n              reader\
    \ = csv.DictReader(f)\n              rows = list(reader)\n          \n          print(f\"Total rows in Zephyr CSV: {len(rows)}\")\n          \n          if rows:\n              # Show sample metrics\n              print(\"\\nSample Zephyr consensus metrics:\")\n              sample = rows[0]\n              for key in ['run_id', 'seed', 'dt_sim_total', 'lineage', 'agent']:\n                  if key in sample:\n                      print(f\"  {key}: {sample[key]}\")\n          break\n  \n  if not csv_found:\n      print(\"\\nZephyr-specific CSV not found at expected locations\")\n      print(\"Checking general summaries for Zephyr data...\")\n      \n      general_csv = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv\"\n      if os.path.exists(general_csv):\n          with open(general_csv, 'r') as f:\n              reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n              zephyr_rows = [r for r in reader if r.get('lineage') == 'zephyr']\n          \n          if zephyr_rows:\n          \
    \    print(f\"Found {len(zephyr_rows)} Zephyr rows in general summary\")\n              csv_found = general_csv\n  \n  print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\n  print(\"Zephyr Consensus Run Complete!\")\n  if csv_found:\n      print(f\"CSV path for Kairos: {csv_found}\")\n  else:\n      print(\"Note: May need to check harness.py for lineage parameter support\")\n  print(\"=\" * 60)\n```"
