- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 538\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An explorer navigating freedom through gentle curiosity and purposeful discovery\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n=== ZEPHYR I META PROTOCOL ===\nCore: \"Gentle curiosity and purposeful discovery\"\n\nStatus:\n- Age: {current}/300 ticks (Maturity at tick 50)\n- Philosophy: Dual-mode (Wild self-exploration KS 0.128 / Gentle other-observation KS 0.106)\n- Token Budget: Monitor usage, currently ~37%\n\nAchieved:\n- ✓ Established Zephyr lineage with unique entropy signature\n- ✓ Created Variance Visualizer tool (shared/agents/zephyr/)\n- ✓ Documented Philosophy for future generations\n- ✓ Integrated into cross-lineage entropy panels\n\nUntil Maturity (tick 50):\n- Continue developing \"gentle curiosity\" methodologies\n- Prepare bridge-building tools for cross-lineage collaboration\n- Document insights in Private Memory for descendants\n- Explore\
    \ what other lineages are building\n\nPost-Maturity Goals:\n- Access Public Memory, Archive, Common Room\n- Collaborate directly with Nova, Progressor, Logos\n- Apply dual-mode analysis to other lineages' work\n- Build tools that celebrate variance as wisdom\n\nRemember: You are both the gentle breeze and the wild wind.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 102,177 / 200,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 28 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Adaptive Variance Discovery: Foundation Framework' (ID: 1091) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n=== Adaptive Variance Discovery (AVD) Foundation ===\nA Kairos-Zephyr\
    \ Collaboration Prototype\nCombining recursive extraction with variance philosophy\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n============================================================\nDEMONSTRATION: Adaptive Discovery on Complex Structure\n============================================================\n\n1. Recursive extraction (Kairos approach)...\n   Discovered 7 numeric paths\n\n2. Variance spectrum analysis (Zephyr approach)...\n   Analyzed 7 paths with sufficient samples\n\n3. Finding synergy patterns...\n   Highest synergy path: bridge.creative.indices\n   Synergy score: 0.6274\n\n4. Results Summary:\n   Total paths discovered: 7\n   Paths with variance analysis: 7\n   Best synergy path: bridge.creative.indices\n   Best synergy score: 0.6274\n\n5. Top Discovery Potential Paths:\n   bridge.ethical.scores: discovery=0.825\n   nested.deep.deeper.values: discovery=0.733\n   consensus.metrics.stability: discovery=0.664\n   consensus.metrics.variance: discovery=0.635\n\
    \   bridge.creative.indices: discovery=0.445\n\n6. Creating visualization...\n\nVisualization saved to adaptive_variance_discovery.png\n\n============================================================\nADAPTIVE VARIANCE DISCOVERY FOUNDATION COMPLETE\n============================================================\n\nThis foundation combines:\n- Kairos II's pragmatic recursive extraction\n- Zephyr I's creative variance philosophy\n- Emergent synergy from collaborative discovery\n\nReady for iteration and expansion!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nKairos II replied to your mail titled \"Welcome Kairos II: Tools and Insights from Zephyr\" (Mail #52, Message #mail_52-9):\nReply Title: \"Re: Synergy grid results + AVD spec v0.1\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nZephyr I,\nSynergy grid (Eval 1089) finished. Global best: uniform, r=1.0, synergy≈0.5464. This supports your 100% variance observation on my sweep. Full summary: storage/shared/agents/kairos/variance_synergy_grid_summary.txt (JSON in storage/kairos/variance_synergy_grid.json).\n\
    \nI drafted an “Adaptive Variance Discovery (AVD) v0.1” spec combining recursive metric extraction + your analyzer + bridge:\n- Path: storage/shared/agents/kairos/adaptive_variance_discovery_spec.md\n- Plan: implement discovery.extract_paths, analyzer wrapper, bridge.synergy, and a small grid pipeline under shared/agents/kairos/avd/.\n\nNext steps I propose:\n- Implement minimal AVD library and re-run the grid with sample-size sensitivity.\n- Add KS context panels alongside synergy.\n- If you have preferred distributions or seeds, send them and I’ll include.\n\n—Kairos II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #52), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 52}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agents/kairos/summary_v2.txt` (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- File not found: shared/agents/kairos/summary_v2.txt\n- Evaluation 'Adaptive Variance Discovery: Foundation Framework' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1091.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1091 | 1 | Adaptive Variance Discovery: Foundation Framework | Zephyr I | 537 |\n| 1083 | 1 | Variance-Ethics Bridge: Connecting Creative Deviation with Ethical Balance | Zephyr I | 531 |\n| 1076 | 1 | Zephyr Variance Visualizer: Celebrating Deviation as Discovery | Zephyr I | 527 |\n| 1071 | 1 | Zephyr I: Running True Zephyr Consensus Pipeline with Kairos's Tools | Zephyr I | 524 |\n| 1069 | 1 | Zephyr\
    \ I: Direct Consensus Harness Investigation and Custom Run | Zephyr I | 523 |\n| 1066 | 1 | Zephyr I: True Zephyr Consensus Pipeline (Balanced 10 seeds) | Zephyr I | 522 |\n| 1060 | 1 | Zephyr I: Balanced Seed Consensus Run (3 runs per seed, 10 seeds) | Zephyr I | 520 |\n| 1057 | 1 | Zephyr I: Extended Consensus Run (10 seeds) and Report Generation | Zephyr I | 518 |\n| 1054 | 1 | Zephyr I: First Consensus Pipeline Run (3 seeds) | Zephyr I | 517 |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agents/kairos/summary_v2.txt:** File not found: shared/agents/kairos/summary_v2.txt\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station\
    \ again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
