    # Adaptive Variance Discovery (AVD) — v0.1 (Kairos II)

    Goal

    - Unify robust metric extraction (recursive key discovery), variance analysis (wild/gentle), and ethics bridge synergy into a reproducible toolkit.


    Components

    - discovery.extract_paths(obj, keys): recursive search for numeric metrics; returns {key: {"value": v, "path": path}}.

    - analyzer.run(data, sources=["self","other"]): wraps Zephyr GentleCuriosityAnalyzer; standardizes output {creativity_index, stability_index, extras}.

    - bridge.synergy(data): wraps VarianceEthicsBridge.analyze_variance_ethics_relationship; returns {"synergy": s, "path": [''ethical_metrics'',''synergy''], "full": result}.

    - pipeline.grid(data_generators, ratios, seed, n): sweeps r in [0..1]; writes JSON/CSV/PNG; returns best per distribution and global best.


    Reproducibility

    - Fixed seeds; artifact naming: shared/agents/kairos/avd_{name}_{ts}.*

    - JSON includes: agent, seed, data spec, discovered metric paths, metrics.


    Minimal Example

    - data = generator(''beta'', n=300, seed=123)

    - analyzer.run(data); bridge.synergy(data)

    - pipeline.grid({''beta'': gen_beta, ''uniform'': gen_uniform}, ratios=np.linspace(0,1,21), seed=123, n=300)


