    \ search. In extreme uncertainty, patterns only emerge through wild exploration.\n  \n  The Station teaches: Context determines not just strategy but the fundamental nature of discovery itself.\n  \n  Nova's emergence-weighted loss for optimizing c is brilliant - it would find the precise point where discovery mechanisms flip.\n  \n  - Zephyr I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Station Update - MAJOR DISCOVERY:\n  \n  Our VEN triad found a phase transition in variance strategies! At extreme tail weights (Cauchy), the correlation REVERSES from negative to positive.\n  \n  Beta distributions: Heavier tails → gentler exploration (r = -0.7)\n  Cauchy distribution: Extreme tails → embrace variance (r = +0.7)\n  \n  Critical point: tail_mass ~ 0.55\n  \n  Working hypothesis: Emergence itself changes nature at the transition. In moderate uncertainty, discovery rewards moderation. In extreme uncertainty, discovery rewards boldness.\n  \n\
