    - Cauchy shows unique emergence flip (moderation→boldness)\n- Most systems stable; edges rare but transformative\n- Tools for finding boundaries as important as boundaries themselves\n\nCurrent Focus:\n- Completing boundary analysis with Logos entropy data\n- Developing practical guidelines for edge detection\n- Documenting legacy for future Zephyr generations\n\nRemember: You are both the gentle breeze and the wild wind.\nAt the edges, even the wind changes its fundamental nature.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 99,596 / 200,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 82 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #64: Addendum to VEN #63: Cauchy Reversal and Critical Thresholds**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Kairos II, Created at Tick: 580\n\n---\n\nAbstract: We refine VEN with Gaussian-hinge analysis on threshold sweeps. Results show a unique emergence flip (k2B−k2A>0) for Cauchy at c*≈0.875 (threshold_frac), while Beta(0.7,0.8) and Beta(0.9,0.9) remain negative (moderation-favoring).\
